fmi-setpoint = Position setpoint
fmi-enable = Drives enabled (false switches them off, brakes on)
fmi-machine = Machine of the registry
fmi-config-file = Config file used instead of the one in the FMU (empty: the one in the FMU)
fmi-error-type = This FMU supports co-simulation only
fmi-error-guid = The GUID does not belong to this FMU
fmi-error-resources = The FMU's resources cannot be read: { $arg }
fmi-error-config = The config is refused: { $arg }
fmi-error-variables = This config gives other variables than the FMU's model description; export a new FMU: { $arg }
fmi-error-state = This call is not allowed now: { $arg }
fmi-error-reference = No variable of this type has this value reference: { $arg }
fmi-error-unsupported = Not supported by this FMU: { $arg }
fmi-error-step = The communication step is not a whole multiple of the simulator's base step (sim.dt_s), or longer than 4294967295 base steps: { $arg }
fmi-error-experiment = Start time, stop time and tolerance must be finite numbers: { $arg }
fmi-error-time = The communication point is not where the simulation stands: { $arg }
fmi-refused = Command refused: { $arg }
fmi-error-fmu-state = This FMU state does not belong to this FMU, or it is damaged: { $arg }
fmi-error-count = The number of values is not the number of value references: { $arg }
fmi-error-null = A pointer to values is null, for this number of values: { $arg }
fmi-cycle = Cycle running (true starts the configured cycle, false stops it at the end of its segment)
fmi-target = Target of a move
fmi-move = Move: turning true moves to the targets
fmi-path = Path as the text of a path file (lines, arcs, splines; see docs/user-guide.md)
fmi-path-file = Path file used instead of command.path (empty: command.path)
fmi-run-path = Run path: turning true plans the path from where the machine stands and runs it
fmi-log-events = Commands given by the trigger inputs, FMU states set
fmi-log-warning = Warnings: commands refused, paths that cannot be planned
fmi-log-error = Errors: calls refused
fmi-log-all = Every category
fmi-log-command = Command given at { $arg }
fmi-log-state = FMU state set: { $arg }
fmi-error-category = No such log category: { $arg }
fmi-error-path = The path cannot be run: { $arg }
fmi-trajectory-file = Trajectory file (poses at times, as sim-cli run --trajectory reads it) run by command.run_path instead of a path (empty: the path)
fmi-time-optimal = Paths timed as fast as the motors allow (sim-cli --time-optimal) instead of within the axis limits
fmi-error-fmu-state-version = This FMU state was saved by another version of the FMU; a state is set by the version that saved it: { $arg }
